# ECS Message System

## Message-Driven Architecture

Use messages for all cross-component communication.

## Defining Messages

Define messages in `constants.ts`:

```typescript
export enum Messages {
  PLAYER_DIED = 'PLAYER_DIED',
  ITEM_COLLECTED = 'ITEM_COLLECTED',
  LEVEL_COMPLETED = 'LEVEL_COMPLETED'
}
```

## Sending Messages

```typescript
// Simple message
this.sendMessage(Messages.PLAYER_DIED);

// Message with data
this.sendMessage(Messages.ITEM_COLLECTED, { 
  itemType: 'coin',
  value: 10 
});

// Message with tag filter (only to objects with tag)
this.sendMessage(Messages.TAKE_DAMAGE, { amount: 10 }, 'enemy');
```

## Receiving Messages

```typescript
class MyComponent extends ECS.Component {
  onInit() {
    // Subscribe to specific messages
    this.subscribe(Messages.PLAYER_DIED);
    this.subscribe(Messages.ITEM_COLLECTED);
    
    // Or subscribe to all messages (use sparingly)
    // this.subscribe(ECS.Messages.ANY);
  }

  onMessage(msg: ECS.Message) {
    switch (msg.action) {
      case Messages.PLAYER_DIED:
        // Handle player death
        break;
      case Messages.ITEM_COLLECTED:
        const { itemType, value } = msg.data;
        // Handle item collection
        break;
    }
  }
}
```

## Message Payload

Access message properties:

```typescript
onMessage(msg: ECS.Message) {
  msg.action;      // Message type
  msg.data;        // Payload data
  msg.component;   // Sender component
  msg.gameObject;  // Associated game object
  msg.responses;   // Collected responses
  msg.expired;     // Stop propagation flag
}
```

## Best Practices

### DO:
- Use messages for all cross-component communication
- Define message types in constants
- Include relevant data in message payload
- Document expected payload structure

### DON'T:
- Don't subscribe to `Messages.ANY` unless absolutely necessary
- Don't send messages in tight loops (performance)
- Don't use messages for internal component logic
- Don't store message references (they can be reused)

## Scene-Level Messages

Send messages from scene or non-component code:

```typescript
scene.sendMessage(Messages.GAME_STARTED, gameData);
```
